# 132 - PRECEDENCE where the wrong ladder yields the OPPOSITE BOOLEAN, in both
# directions:
#   line 1  true or (false and false)  == true   <- correct, and binds tighter
#           (true or false) and false  == false  <- flat left-to-right
#   line 2  (false and true) or true   == true   <- correct
#           false and (true or true)   == false  <- if `or` bound tighter
# Both lines are true; each is false under a different specific mistake, so the
# pair distinguishes the correct ladder from either way of getting it wrong.
--- source
print true or false and false;
print false and true or true;
--- expect
true
true
